# Real-Time Status Monitoring Fix

The pipeline **is definitely working** (as proven by your 100% GPU usage and 7,500 frames created), but the UI looks frozen because our status reporter is waiting for a "New Line" before it updates. In long renders, MuseTalk stays on the same line for 20 minutes using "Carriage Returns" (\r).

This plan fixes the reporting "heartbeat" so you always know exactly where it is.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> This change only affects **how the progress is reported to you**—it does not change the actual AI rendering (which is already working optimally on your GPU).

## Proposed Changes

### [Engine Core]

#### [MODIFY] [lipsync_musetalk.py](file:///C:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/lipsync_musetalk.py)
- **Non-Blocking Reader**: Replace `readline()` (which blocks on `\n`) with a character-based reader that catches `\r`.
- **Progress Heartbeat**: Ensure the `tqdm` percentage from the child process is passed to the Gradio UI immediately.
- **Improved Scraper**: Update the phase detection keywords to be more sensitive to the actual MuseTalk output stream.

